.Dd April 25, 2026
.Dt PKGBASE-BUILD 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkgbase-build
.Nd FreeBSD base system package build system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
Build targets:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Cm make stage-packages
.It
.Cm make create-packages
.It
.Cm make sign-packages
.It
.Cm make packages
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
system creates binary packages from the FreeBSD base system,
enabling package-based updates using
.Xr pkg 8 .
.Pp
The build process consists of three main phases:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Em Staging :
Files are collected into staging directories
.It
.Em Creation :
Package files are generated from staged content
.It
.Em Signing :
Repository metadata is cryptographically signed
.El
.Sh BUILD TARGETS
.Ss Staging Targets
.Bl -tag -width "stage-packages-world" -compact
.It Cm stage-packages-world
Stage userland files into
.Pa ${WSTAGEDIR} .
.It Cm stage-packages-kernel
Stage kernel files into
.Pa ${KSTAGEDIR} .
.It Cm stage-packages-source
Stage source files into
.Pa ${SSTAGEDIR} .
.It Cm stage-packages
Run all staging targets.
.El
.Ss Creation Targets
.Bl -tag -width "create-packages-world" -compact
.It Cm create-packages-world
Create world component packages.
.It Cm create-packages-kernel
Create kernel packages.
.It Cm create-packages-source
Create source packages.
.It Cm create-packages-sets
Create metapackages grouping related packages.
.It Cm create-packages
Run all package creation targets.
.El
.Ss Signing Targets
.Bl -tag -width "sign-packages" -compact
.It Cm sign-packages
Sign repository metadata and create signature file.
.El
.Ss Complete Build
.Bl -tag -width "packages" -compact
.It Cm packages
Run complete package build: stage, create, and sign.
.It Cm update-packages
Build only changed packages (incremental).
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The following variables control the build process:
.Ss Package Naming
.Bl -tag -width "PKG_WORKERS_COUNT" -compact
.It Va PKG_NAME_PREFIX
Package name prefix (default:
.Dq FreeBSD ).
.It Va PKG_MAINTAINER
Maintainer contact email (default:
.Dq re@FreeBSD.org ).
.It Va PKG_WWW
Project website URL (default:
.Dq https://www.FreeBSD.org ).
.El
.Ss Build Control
.Bl -tag -width "PKG_WORKERS_COUNT" -compact
.It Va PKG_WORKERS_COUNT
Parallel workers for signing (default: 1).
.It Va SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Timestamp for reproducible builds.
.El
.Ss Directories
.Bl -tag -width "PKG_WORKERS_COUNT" -compact
.It Va WSTAGEDIR
World staging directory.
.It Va KSTAGEDIR
Kernel staging directory.
.It Va SSTAGEDIR
Source staging directory.
.It Va REPODIR
Package repository output directory.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "tools/pkgbase/build/" -compact
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/vars.mk
Configuration variables.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/common.mk
Shared functions and directory definitions.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/bootstrap.mk
Tool bootstrapping.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/stage.mk
Staging targets.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/create.mk
Package creation targets.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/sign.mk
Repository signing.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/build/update.mk
Update package logic.
.It Pa tools/pkgbase/metalog_reader.lua
METALOG analysis tool.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Complete Build
Build all packages:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cd /usr/src
make packages
.Ed
.Ss Step-by-Step Build
Build in phases with inspection between:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make stage-packages
# Inspect ${WSTAGEDIR}
make create-packages
make sign-packages
.Ed
.Ss Dry Run
See what would be built without executing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make -n packages
.Ed
.Sh METALOG FORMAT
The METALOG file records file metadata during staging:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
./bin/ls type=file uname=root gname=wheel mode=0755 \\
    tags=package=FreeBSD-utilities
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Nm metalog_reader.lua
tool analyzes these files.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr build 7 ,
.Xr pkg 8 ,
.Xr src.conf 5 ,
.Xr style.Makefile 5
.Sh HISTORY
The modular build system was introduced to improve maintainability
and enable future enhancements like parallel builds and dependency tracking.
